      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name} \"The VRChat app downloads and replaces yt-dlp.exe with VRChat's own custom downstream fork of yt-dlp (currently version 2026.01.29) on every app launch, ...\" is wrong.\n\nIt downloads whenever you join a world, and the scripts checking for the hash of the yt-dlp.exe, if it is mismatching, it will simply redownload the executable, while you are loading your desired world.\n\nReplacing the file on each boot (which was a nonsense to deal with in the first place, as VRChat devs could have simply updated their fork beforehand, which they don't, and if, then way too late, so a second time it gets broken by google), won't work anymore.",
